<%- include('../partials/info-start', { crumb: 'Company', eyebrow: 'Careers', heading: 'The team we’d build.', intro: 'Willow is a fictional company, so there are no open roles and no applications to send. This page describes how a team behind a product like this would work.' }) %>
            <section class="info-section" id="status">
                <h2>No open positions</h2>
                <p>Willow Banking Corp. does not employ anyone and is not hiring. If you received a job offer, interview request or payment request that mentions Willow, it did not come from this project — please treat it as a possible scam and do not share personal details.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="how">
                <h2>How we would work</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Small, cross-functional teams</strong> owning a customer outcome end to end — from “send money abroad” to “understand my net worth”.</li>
                    <li><strong>Security and accessibility as defaults,</strong> reviewed in every change rather than bolted on before launch.</li>
                    <li><strong>Plain-language writing</strong> treated as part of the product. A confusing fee notice is a bug.</li>
                    <li><strong>Evidence before opinion.</strong> Prototypes, usability sessions and measured outcomes guide decisions.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
            <section class="info-section" id="disciplines">
                <h2>Disciplines a real Willow would need</h2>
                <p>Product design, frontend and backend engineering, security engineering, data and analytics, risk and compliance, financial operations, customer support and content design. A regulated bank would also need licensed leadership, independent audit and a compliance function long before its first customer.</p>
            </section>
